	ATLAS_MGR_TITLE = "Atlas Manager",
	AUTHOR_WORDS = "Greetings from the author of Kingdom Rush Dove!\nKingdom Rush Dove is a completely free Kingdom Rush mod developed with the goals of high performance, high playability, high balance and high freedom. Any commercial use of this mod is an infringement. If you paid to get this game, the person who provided it to you is definitely a scammer.\nBefore playing, you absolutely need to understand the following. Please read it carefully and complete the test. Any question asked of others about the content below wastes other people's time, and wasting other people's time is \"no different from murdering them for their money\". If you are worried that you will not remember it, take screenshots for later use. Closing this page means you have fully understood everything on it and agree to take responsibility for all consequences of not following it.\n1. Before playing Kingdom Rush Dove, you are advised to first play at least one original Kingdom Rush game.\n2. Kingdom Rush Dove inherits the classic design of the first three games. Advanced towers are divided into four branches, all upgraded from level-3 towers. Each advanced tower is unlocked after beating a specific level, and once unlocked it can be used freely in non-Iron levels.\n3. Kingdom Rush Dove introduces a two-hero mechanic while inheriting the hero system of the first game: all heroes level up from level 1 within a match, and hero levels are not kept outside of a match. There are two reasons for this: first, starting with two level-10 heroes makes the early defense rely too heavily on heroes; second, in-match leveling provides more parameters that can be balanced. If you dislike this design, you can press f1 on the world map to open the config and select \"Start heroes at max level\".\n4. To prevent two heroes from steamrolling the main campaign, early main-line levels have reduced hero experience gain.\n5. The hotkeys for summoning heroes 1-5 are a,d,s,q,r.\n6. Press f to summon all reinforcements, and press e to summon all summonable units other than reinforcements, heroes and barracks soldiers (such as the summonable units explicitly described in a hero's skill description). On Android, you can instead tap the reinforcements skill while it is on cooldown to summon all reinforcements.\n7. If you notice the game stuttering, consider lowering the frame rate. For reference, the original games run at 30/60 FPS. On PC, it is recommended to select the highest frame rate first and then choose one that suits your performance; on Android, 30 or 60 FPS is recommended. You can also press f10 in a match to view the current frame rate and decide on a suitable one.\n8. The game speed keys are: 4 to slow down, 5 to speed up, 6 to reset. If the game seems very slow, you may have pressed one by accident; please reset it manually.\n9. If the image quality looks poor, your resolution choice may be unsuitable. You can turn off fullscreen, try resolutions one by one until the game screen size roughly matches your screen size, then restore fullscreen, and the image quality should be restored.\n10. Scroll the mouse wheel (middle button) to zoom the screen.\n11. Search for 时笺滴答 on bilibili to find clear videos of all the author's custom levels.\n12. The f1 key on the world map has many more freely configurable options; adjust them as you see fit. For numeric options, you can click them and type a value with the keyboard.\n13. In a match you can press f1 to enable one-click tower building and f4 to summon heroes (both must be enabled in the world map UI settings), f5 to start the next wave, f6 to gain 99999 gold, and f7 to gain 100 lives.\n14. The Hero Hall and the tower codex provide buttons for viewing detailed mechanics and stats.\n15. If the game aborts and reports an error, please: a. make sure you are on the latest version; b. take a complete screenshot of the game when it aborted; c. add a detailed written description of when the game aborted, what you were doing at the time and what the game was doing; then send your feedback.\n16. If you think you have found a bug, please: a. make sure you are on the latest version; b. take a complete screenshot of the bug when it occurs; c. take a complete screenshot of the small black console window that appears alongside the game; d. add a detailed written description; then send your feedback.\n17. If you run into an update error, please: a. screenshot the update error; b. screenshot the directory structure of your game installation (you can open the game installation folder in a file manager and take a screenshot); c. add a detailed written description; then send your feedback.\n18. If you do not follow the feedback requirements above, you will very likely be scolded and blocked.\n19. The complete update history of the game can be found at https://krdovedownload4.crazyspotteddove.top/history. If you ask about the update history, you will very likely be scolded and blocked.\n20. If you are forced to re-download and reinstall Kingdom Rush Dove, rest assured that your saves are preserved. On mobile, simply download the new package to update; do not delete the old one.\n21. Kingdom Rush Dove does not aim to give mobile users the complete game experience; it only provides the most basic play service, on the premise that it adds no pressure whatsoever to PC development. As for mobile, the author's stance is: no bug reports from mobile are accepted, but game abort error messages from mobile are accepted. For the sake of your own play experience, please play Kingdom Rush Dove on PC whenever conditions allow.\n22. Kingdom Rush Dove does not accept any requests to hurry up development. If you insist on asking for updates, you will very likely be scolded and blocked.\n23. Please read the changelog carefully; it may contain important warnings. If you play already-described unfinished content like a daredevil, hit an error, and then ask what happened, you will very likely be scolded and blocked.\n24. Every mod has its own design and gameplay features; disparaging other mods is strictly forbidden. If you can, please support the original game.\n25. Kingdom Rush Dove improves stat displays: after clicking a unit, the green circle shows the ranged range, the blue circle shows the blocking range, the first attack stat is the basic attack, and the second is the ranged attack or skill.\n26. Kingdom Rush Dove damage types: let the target's physical armor be a and its magic armor be b (a and b are in the domain [0, 1]). When damage is resolved, the final damage value is the original value * (1 - resistance). Different damage types use different resistance formulas. Brutal damage and explosion damage: the resistance formula is a * (0.2a + 0.4); impale: deals double the panel damage, but the resistance formula is a * (2 - a); magic explosion damage: the resistance formula is b * (0.2b + 0.4); lightning damage: the resistance formula is 0.5a; gunshot damage: the resistance formula is 0.7a; mixed damage: when b > a the resistance is a, otherwise it is (a + b) * 0.5.\n27. The brutal damage icon is a claw, the true damage icon is a golden cross, the lightning damage icon is a lightning bolt, the magic explosion damage icon is a blue radial burst, the mixed damage icon is a sword with blue on it, the armor-breaking damage icon is a shattered white shield, the magic-breaking damage icon is a shattered blue shield, and the impale icon is a red impact shape.\n28. Armor-breaking / magic-breaking damage: on top of the physical / magic damage, additionally deals 2 * original damage value * resistance² as true damage.\n29. On Veteran difficulty, tower prices increase, heroes level up more slowly, and the pace tightens after wave 6; on Impossible difficulty, enemy stats are higher, high-HP enemies gain some instant-kill resistance, and enemy stats keep increasing after wave 6.\n30. The author does not accept any modification suggestions unless the author asks for them.\n31. Kingdom Rush Dove promises that its network connection is used only to provide update services and will not collect any user privacy data.\n32. On the launch screen you can configure which IP protocol is used for updates. IPv6 is faster and preferred. If your network does not support IPv6, you can switch to IPv4. If you are unfamiliar with these terms, you can select IPv6 first and then wait. The updater will automatically detect your network environment and choose a suitable protocol (this will take some time). If you are launching while offline, please turn off updates on the launch screen.\n33. On the world map, press f1 to open the config, f2 to open the cricket-fighting config (requires a modding background, see the official site for details), f3 to open the plugin manager, f4 to open UI settings, k to open key bindings, l to open launch options, and 1, 2, 3, 5 to switch maps, with wasd to move the view. The launch options let you turn off the author's words.\n34. Kingdom Rush Dove supports a plugin store, so plugins can be installed directly in-game. If you install manually, place the plugin folder in plugins under the save directory. In-game, press f3 on the world map to open the plugin manager and choose which plugins to enable.\n35. On Android, functions bound to hotkeys can be used by tapping the pause button in a match. On the world map, view them by tapping the gear icon in the top-left corner.\n36. Kingdom Rush Dove includes damage number and healing number displays, but they are off by default. To enable them, click the gear icon in the top-left corner of the world map, find UI settings, and turn them on there.\n37. On Android, a language selection screen appears at startup, where you can switch languages. If you do not want to see it on every launch, tap the gear icon in the top-left corner of the world map, open Launch Options, and turn on Skip Language Selection.\n38. Press t in a match to open the time rewind panel (rebindable in key bindings; the pause menu and the victory/defeat screens also have a Time rewind button, which is how you reach it on Android): drag the timeline to pick the moment to go back to; each wave's start is a tick mark on it, and it shows both the current and the target game time. Dragging to the far right replays everything from the start; release the mouse to start rewinding. Leave the panel with its Close button, or with Esc / t (use Close on Android). Rewinding clears all recorded operations after that moment, and  the result is not guaranteed to be exactly the same as before.\n",
